=====================

 S~S This Repository

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What is the purpose of the objects in this repository or repo?

    * The repo contains an example of the simplest or most basic SimpleSal App: display the Time.

      * Even the simplest of Apps may be configurable at build time.  This App will either set
            "the Current Time" as: zero, or, the Time at which the software was built (BuiltAt).

            In the former, the numbers displayed appear to be a count-up timer, from zero.
            In the latter, the numbers displayed appear to be a strange clock, showing the Time.

        This variation between two different functionalities is managed through a build-time option.

        The alternative would require two repos, each with an App identical except in name and
        a few lines of source code difference in the App: Time initialization to zero or BuiltAt.

    * Quick explanation of the value being displayed by the App:

        [flags|days.hours.minutes.seconds.milliseconds.microseconds.nanoseconds.plancks]

        plancks and nanoseconds are not detectable, microseconds accuracy is platform-specific.

        Guessing the meaning of the flags is an exercise for the reader: what is a good Time? Is it
        the Time value itself that is good, meaning all of the values in each Time unit are valid?
        "We had a good time" describes what happened between a starting Time and an ending Time.

    * One method of display allows a user to attempt to interact faster than other humans interact
      (continuously clearing the screen in the IDE Serial Monitor is hard to do faster than 100ms).

    * The other method of display adds a Line Feed to the Carriage Return emitted by method #1
      (the current value always is visible at the bottom of the IDE Serial screen auto-scrolling).

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What are the contents of this repository?

   * "rr\" means "repository root\"

   * The managed object is the rr\app-time\app-time.ino" file in the rr\app-time\ directory
     and several files in the rr\app-time\SimpleSal directory (see configuration methods).

       * this App works with any version of SimpleSal,

            therefore there IS NO NEED for rr\app-time\SimpleSal\      (in the App repo)

         * this App uses the configuration method where ".start" files are renamed and used as-is,
           in addition this App places the "*.h" version of the "*.start" files with those files
           in the rr\app-time\SimpleSal\ directory.  The files are owned by the App, not SimpleSal.

       * rr\app-time\app-time.ino

       * because this App does not initiate any Events, the ssTEA helper for the API ia not used

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What happens in my workspace as a result of interacting with this repository?

    The managed object will be placed into your workspace, along with the human metadata files
    (depending on your ability to configure the repo App to only consider files matching filters).

    This configuration method results in files in the same directory from multiple repository roots.

    The only reason to have a metadata copy locally is if files are being modified for a release.

------------------------------------------

 S~S  What about the version of the SimpleSal software the App co-exists with?

    This specific version of app-time is part of a coherent SimpleSal-wide release of software.

    At a minimum, this SimpleSal App will build with any SimpleSal version
        released as or released after "V1.0.0" of 2026/10/16.

------------------------------------------

